// Panel contents: binds engine / game / smoke / camera settings to UI controls — the game's ONE tweak panel (Tab), laid out for ui/panel.ts v2:
// SYSTEMS down the rail in the picture's pipeline order (Frame · Direct · Indirect · Volumetrics · Materials · Denoiser · Renderer fx), then the world's
// (Weather & wind · Effects), then the Sandbox and the tools (Destruction · Audio · Checkpoints); on each page SECTIONS made of the old flat groups split
// along the prefixes their rows already carried ('taau:', 'sharp:', 'restir:', 'shadow:' / 'gi:' / 'spec:', 'wind:', 'wet:', 'aim ▸', 'chaos ▸' …),
// each with a live one-line summary in its header and a '↺' where a shipped-defaults table exists. Rows built inside adv(…) are A/B-only knobs: out of the
// way until 'all knobs'. Where a knob TABLE is bound row after row the same way (get / set that key, save, the shipped value for the revert dot) the rows are
// a declarative spec through knobRows(); anything with logic of its own stays written out. Every row the flat panel had is still here under the same label,
// range, tooltip and side effects — tools/qa/panel-inventory.ts (probes.ts panel-inventory) holds that against main's frozen list.
